      "Evidence": "The story braids all five pillars organically: neuretics deliver manifests and IdentiScan flags mid-scene; nanite carapaces (\u0027Mama\u0027/\u0027the Kid\u0027) repair and harvest bodies as routine infrastructure; Ekow is a fully agentive AI-adjacent... wait, Ekow is human, but the Tears/neuretics divide (Levin\u0027s drug-augmented driving vs Tomas\u0027s neuretic overlays) marks the cognitive-augmentation class divide, Carrion operates as the de facto governing law over financed bodies, and the Schism appears physically (\u0027a two-inch orbit of gravel turned slowly in the air \u2014 a little schism, months old\u0027 and \u0027the white gap every map printed... the air beyond it leaning in a direction that made Tomas put his eyes back on the road\u0027).",
      "Fix": "Introduce at least one clearly agentive AI faction with its own stakes (distinct from human characters and background tech) so pillar one isn\u0027t left implicit through absence, since Ekow, Levin, and Tomas are all human and the AI presence is currently confined to passive tools like Mama and IdentiScan."
